# Draft code owners: which team owns which path (specs/DREAMFERENCE_ORGANISATION.md §2 and §4.2).
#
# Inert where it is: GitHub reads CODEOWNERS only from the repository's root, docs/ or .github/,
# so this file changes nothing until rollout Phase 2 moves it to .github/CODEOWNERS, after the
# teams exist in the organisation. scripts/as_team.py reads it today to say which teams must
# review a change.
#
# Syntax is GitHub's: a pattern, then one or more owners. The last matching line wins, so the
# fallback comes first and the narrowest paths come last. Every owner is a GitHub team; the
# teams' bots (dreamference-<team>[bot]) cannot be code owners, because GitHub allows only users
# and teams here.

# Fallback: anything not named below.
